  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The unchanged (MnNiSi)0.62(FeCoGe)0.38 alloy has a large caloric response.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The unchanged alloy has poor compressive strength and crack-prone mechanical integrity.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The intervention is an approximately 2–3 at.% Cu addition.",
      "field": "intervention",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 2–3 at.% Cu will form a fine, dispersed Cu-rich ductile second phase.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Adding 2–3 at.% Cu may refine the alloy's grain structure.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "A finely dispersed ductile phase can improve stress distribution and mechanical integrity in a multiphase high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7021732::web::023::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cu-rich phase will arrest crack propagation by absorbing and redistributing local stresses.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Crack arrest and stress redistribution will operate during the caloric phase transformation.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Phase-specific ductile and brittle constituents can contribute differently to the bulk mechanical response of a multiphase high-entropy alloy.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7021732::web::023::conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Alloying-induced solid-solution and second-phase changes can alter compressive strength and plastic strain in high-entropy alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7512535::web::030::5_summary"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is supported by phase-engineering strategies from related shape-memory and magnetocaloric alloys.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cu addition will increase compressive strength to above 200 MPa.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cu addition will reduce cracking relative to the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cu-alloyed material's isothermal entropy change will remain within the same order of magnitude as that of the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Cu-alloyed material's adiabatic temperature change will remain within the same order of magnitude as that of the unchanged alloy.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The hypothesis is intended to apply under magnetic fields up to a few tesla, operational barocaloric pressures, transformation-active temperatures, and compressive loading.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The modified alloy remains rare-earth-free.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": false,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
